From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ESP32-S31 Linux <s31-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] a2dp: request short LE interval for the bulk stream

The stock 45 ms / 420 ms link drops under load (9 missed 45 ms anchors in
a 400 ms RF hole: supervision timeout, reason 0x08) and caps streaming.
Ask the central for 7.5-15 ms interval, zero latency, 2000 ms supervision
when streaming starts.  No other link parameters change in this stage.
---
 example/a2dp_sink_demo.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/example/a2dp_sink_demo.c
+++ b/example/a2dp_sink_demo.c
@@ -416,6 +416,14 @@
             little_endian_read_16(buffer, 0) == GATT_CLIENT_CHARACTERISTICS_CONFIGURATION_NOTIFICATION;
         printf("S31 BLE stream: notifications %s\n", s31_ble_stream_subscribed ? "enabled" : "disabled");
         if (s31_ble_stream_subscribed){
+            /* Stage B: ask the central for a short interval (7.5-15 ms)
+             * with a tolerant supervision timeout (2000 ms).  The stock
+             * 45 ms / 420 ms link misses 9 anchors in a 400 ms RF hole
+             * and drops under load; shorter intervals also multiply
+             * streaming throughput. */
+            gap_request_connection_parameter_update(con_handle, 6, 12, 0, 200);
+        }
+        if (s31_ble_stream_subscribed){
             s31_ble_stream_seq = 0;
             s31_ble_stream_notifies = 0;
             s31_ble_stream_bytes = 0;
-- 
2.43.0
